{"answer": "The spec (FR-003) first called for a `switch` over `EscalationTrigger` with no `default`. As built, the exhaustiveness fixture, `apps/api/test/fixtures/escalationTriggers.ts`, is a `Record<EscalationTrigger, TriggerSource>` that uses a `satisfies` clause. There are two reasons. First, it gives the same guarantee: a member added without an entry fails `npm run typecheck`, and so does an extra member. Second, a switch with a case for every one of the ten triggers exceeds the lint complexity limit. Typechecking of `apps/api/test/**` has covered this fixture since #275.", "sources": ["specs/support-agent-escalation/spec.md (FR-002, FR-003)", "apps/api/src/escalation/triggers.ts", "docs/human-oversight.md"]}
```

